"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"The \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"query_wait_timeout\"}],\" setting is a PgBouncer configuration option that determines the maximum time a query can wait in the queue before being executed. Neon’s default value for this setting is \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"120 seconds\"}],\". If a query exceeds this timeout while in the queue, it will not be executed. For more details about this setting, refer to \",[\"$\",\"$L62\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/connect/connection-pooling#neon-pgbouncer-configuration-settings\",\"children\":\"Neon PgBouncer configuration settings\"}],\".\"]}]\nb0:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"To avoid this error, we recommend reviewing your workload. If it includes batch processing with \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"UPDATE\"}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"INSERT\"}],\" statements, review their performance. Slow queries may be the root cause. Try optimizing these queries to reduce execution time, which can help prevent them from exceeding the timeout.\"]}]\nb1:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Alternatively, Neon can increase the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"query_wait_timeout\"}],\" value for you, but this is not typically recommended, as increasing the timeout can lead to higher latency or blocked queries under heavy workloads.\"]}]\nb2:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"the-request-could-not-be-authorized-due-to-an-internal-error\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"The request could not be authorized due to an internal error\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#the-request-could-not-be-authorized-due-to-an-intern